{
  "dom_id": "step-q236899",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed cosine function with a minimum value of $6$ and a maximum value of $10.$",
  "worked_solution": "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{6+10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=8.$",
